(7244167, 1123607, 21304, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by giantmike:</b></div><hr/><i> Well, an interesting turn of events. This photo will certainly be heralded as a photo that very obviously does not meet challenge, yet gets a ribbon. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>It''s interesting, I had only noticed that something was different after I had submitted the photo and let my TPL team know which one it was. The ball was blue initially, but de-saturated, the feather white, and shot on a reflective black background... I didn''t even think that there could be any "colour" in the photo. I''m still intrigued by the whole thing - don''t have more time to investigate or write more now. But interesting input, and thanks for all the votes (including you, Mike)</td>', 'Originally posted by giantmike: Well, an interesting turn of events. This photo will certainly be heralded as a photo that very obviously does not meet challenge, yet gets a ribbon.   It''s interesting, I had only noticed that something was different after I had submitted the photo and let my TPL team know which one it was. The ball was blue initially, but de-saturated, the feather white, and shot on a reflective black background... I didn''t even think that there could be any "colour" in the photo. I''m still intrigued by the whole thing - don''t have more time to investigate or write more now. But interesting input, and thanks for all the votes (including you, Mike)', '2014-07-25 09:51:02.000000', NULL, 0),
